  {
   "id": "vYRhbcqVDAAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2018-02-28T11:11:46Z",
   "subject": "Re: monteCarloMed bug with subtraction",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>It looks like a bug in the code. I&#39;ll get it fixed ASAP. </div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>The problem is the<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> uniquepar() </font>function defined within the<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> monteCarloMed() </font>function.  It only looks for &quot;<font face=\"courier new, monospace\">+</font>&quot; and &quot;<font face=\"courier new, monospace\">*</font>&quot; operators, so it thinks &quot;<font face=\"courier new, monospace\">b1-a1</font>&quot; is the variable name rather than &quot;<font face=\"courier new, monospace\">b1</font>&quot;.  </div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> uniquepar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;a1*b1-a1*b2&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;a1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;b1-a1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;b2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div><div>Given that some indirect effects involve more complex functions (e.g., when outcomes are binary, but we&#39;d like to see a CI for indirect effects in an odds-ratio metric: see slide 25 <a href=\"http://www.da.ugent.be/cvs/pages/en/Presentations/Presentation%20Yves%20Rosseel.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.da.ugent.be/cvs/pages/en/Presentations/Presentation%2520Yves%2520Rosseel.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792425986889000&amp;usg=AOvVaw15W3aZCovfSiZA_Qgcyt5a\">here</a>), it would be nice if the function were more general, allowing any R expression that can be calculated on the sampled parameters.  <br></div><div><br></div><div>I propose we get rid of the<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> uniquepar() </font>function and replace line 153</div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">paramnames </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> uniquepar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">expression</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br></font></div><div>with this:<br></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">paramnames </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> all</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">vars</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">formula</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">paste</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;~&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> expression</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span></div></code></div><br>It would work with Mauricio&#39;s example:</div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div></div></code></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">med </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;a1*b1 - a1*b2&#39;</span></div></code></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>all</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">vars</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">formula</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">paste</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;~&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> med</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;a1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;b1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;b2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><div><div><br></div></div><div>and in more general cases (e.g., with <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">log()</font>, <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">pnorm()</font>, or<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> ^</font>):</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">all</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">vars</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">formula</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">paste</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;~&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> med</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;a1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;b1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;b2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Postdoctoral Researcher, Methods and Statistics</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">UvA web page: <a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792425986889000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0KwYxzMaw4vw1L93nCQO4G\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "f_gm1YsBAwAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2018-03-08T12:44:14Z",
   "subject": "Re: monteCarloMed bug with subtraction",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\">paramnames </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> all</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">vars</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">formula</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">paste</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;~&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> expression</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span></code></div></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I pushed this change, and Mauricio&#39;s example works in the latest development version (0.4-15.914) available on github.</div></div>"
    ],
